WEBVTT

00:00.007 --> 00:01.674
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION. UNDERAGE
DRINKING IS STRONGLY PROHIBITED.

00:01.675 --> 00:03.343
FORCEFUL ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION AND
SHAMEFUL ACTS ARE NOT ENCOURAGED.

00:03.344 --> 00:04.970
VIEW THIS AS A COMEDY. ALL CHARACTERS
APPEARING IN THIS WORK ARE OF LEGAL AGE.

00:10.267 --> 00:13.895
Let's ride out into the
highway of our youth

00:13.896 --> 00:16.899
Right now is always
the best of the season

00:17.107 --> 00:20.652
Get high on hope, as
we adults keep winning

00:20.653 --> 00:24.113
Let's take a dive to explore
an entirely new world

00:24.114 --> 00:27.450
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 2

00:27.451 --> 00:29.537
Ever Endless

00:30.746 --> 00:32.414
Ever Endless

00:34.166 --> 00:35.709
Ever Endless

00:37.586 --> 00:38.963
Ever Endless

00:39.630 --> 00:44.425
Mon-Tues-Weds-Thurs-Fri,
my life knows no variety

00:44.426 --> 00:45.845
Ever Endless

00:46.262 --> 00:51.057
Sat-Sun, wake up in the afternoon
with only my smartphone to surf

00:51.058 --> 00:52.642
Ever Endless

00:52.643 --> 00:54.060
All my limbs' been giving in

00:54.061 --> 00:55.895
Kalbi's a burden
like my lumber spine

00:55.896 --> 00:57.480
Doing family
service with irises dim

00:57.481 --> 00:59.108
But you know that
I'll go all the way

00:59.525 --> 01:02.695
Glitter, shimmer,
the light's shining

01:02.987 --> 01:06.531
Let's give it one more chance

01:06.532 --> 01:09.994
Let's ride out into the
highway of our youth

01:10.202 --> 01:12.997
Right now is always
the best of the season

01:13.205 --> 01:16.833
Get high on hope, as
we adults keep winning

01:16.834 --> 01:19.837
Let's take a dive to explore
an entirely new world

01:20.087 --> 01:22.213
Youth is when you never...

01:22.214 --> 01:23.715
stop chasing your own values

01:23.716 --> 01:25.383
Our youth's eternal

01:25.384 --> 01:26.968
the color never fades with age

01:26.969 --> 01:28.845
Youth is when you keep...

01:28.846 --> 01:30.388
getting lost along the way

01:30.389 --> 01:33.934
Youth is Forever

01:35.644 --> 01:37.354
It's so unfair.

01:37.605 --> 01:38.397
- Huh?
- Huh?

01:39.148 --> 01:41.566
Um... What are
you talking about?

01:41.567 --> 01:43.527
Our club's drinking parties.

01:43.861 --> 01:47.614
It's always the guys
only who get to go wild.

01:47.615 --> 01:48.990
That's true.

01:48.991 --> 01:52.119
Don't you join them
often too, Azusa-san?

01:52.536 --> 01:55.956
So today, we're going
to party hard, just us girls.

01:56.123 --> 01:57.666
A girls' party, right?

01:57.958 --> 01:58.499
NANAKA'S ROOM

01:58.500 --> 02:00.460
Are we doing it in my room?

02:00.461 --> 02:02.129
It'll be more fun
that way, right?

02:02.796 --> 02:04.256
What about Nanaka's room?

02:04.423 --> 02:06.258
Absolutely not.

02:07.259 --> 02:08.426
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

02:08.427 --> 02:10.803
Woo! This is what a
normal drinking party's like.

02:10.804 --> 02:12.181
I'm glad.

02:13.098 --> 02:15.725
Doesn't it feel a bit
hollow to you, Azusa-san?

02:15.726 --> 02:18.687
Not at all, I'm a maiden too.

02:18.979 --> 02:21.607
But speaking of lacking...

02:21.774 --> 02:22.774
What is it?

02:22.775 --> 02:25.443
Chii-chan's room doesn't
have any decorations.

02:25.444 --> 02:27.404
I was thinking the same thing.

02:27.696 --> 02:29.740
I think this is fine, though.

02:29.990 --> 02:32.325
But you do have makeup.

02:32.326 --> 02:34.494
My sister just put that there.

02:34.495 --> 02:38.164
Because whether I leave her alone,
Chisa-chan wouldn't do anything.

02:38.165 --> 02:39.707
That's kinda true.

02:39.708 --> 02:42.377
Well, it's okay if
it's just makeup...

02:42.378 --> 02:43.879
Is there anything else?

02:44.797 --> 02:46.589
A girls' party in Chisa's room?

02:46.590 --> 02:48.801
So could you bring
this up to them?

02:49.844 --> 02:51.053
Chisa.

02:51.470 --> 02:53.596
Uncle gave you some...

02:53.597 --> 02:55.975
She even went and got me this.

03:02.815 --> 03:04.107
Listen to me!

03:04.108 --> 03:05.024
Ah, okay.

03:05.025 --> 03:07.026
That was something
my sister bought.

03:07.027 --> 03:08.821
I do not own it.

03:08.946 --> 03:10.154
Is that so?

03:10.155 --> 03:11.323
Do you really get it?

03:12.157 --> 03:14.076
It's fine, I understand.

03:14.410 --> 03:16.786
As expected of something
Nanaka-san would buy.

03:16.787 --> 03:18.664
He definitely doesn't get it.

03:19.748 --> 03:20.958
What happened?

03:21.166 --> 03:23.585
I feel a little guilty.

03:23.586 --> 03:24.336
Guilty?

03:24.837 --> 03:26.964
About not keeping my promise.

03:27.756 --> 03:29.257
Thanks, Chisa.

03:29.258 --> 03:32.428
Next time, I'll buy you some
sexier underwear as thanks.

03:33.637 --> 03:36.307
I don't really get it, but
that's definitely not good.

03:38.058 --> 03:39.017
Welcome back.

03:39.018 --> 03:41.436
- Did you clear up the confusion?
- I think so.

03:41.437 --> 03:43.898
I could hear your
voice from here.

03:44.064 --> 03:47.401
But saying this belongs
to Nanaka is unbelievable.

03:47.651 --> 03:48.277
Huh?

03:51.447 --> 03:54.283
I think that God
is very ignoble.

03:54.617 --> 03:57.243
Why are ours so small?

03:57.244 --> 03:58.078
"Ours?"

03:59.079 --> 04:00.581
Why is that, I wonder?

04:00.748 --> 04:02.916
Do you do anything special?

04:02.917 --> 04:04.793
Like exercise or
eating something?

04:05.044 --> 04:07.879
Well, if I had to say...

04:07.880 --> 04:09.673
isn't it from doing
"naughty" things?

04:10.674 --> 04:11.967
R-Really?

04:12.176 --> 04:15.095
Breast growth is thanks
to female hormones, right?

04:15.721 --> 04:17.430
So to boost those hormones...

04:17.431 --> 04:19.767
that kind of stimulation
is the best way.

04:20.518 --> 04:22.937
That actually makes sense.

04:23.479 --> 04:25.439
Huh? Then what about her?

04:26.440 --> 04:27.148
Huh?

04:27.149 --> 04:29.275
Ah, as for Nanaka...

04:29.276 --> 04:31.445
It's because she's
full of familial love.

04:32.655 --> 04:35.574
Basically, stimulation
is very important.

04:35.699 --> 04:37.367
That's why...

04:37.368 --> 04:38.160
Huh?

04:38.327 --> 04:40.287
- Eh he he.
- Heh? Huh?

04:40.454 --> 04:42.498
Iori, take this up too.

04:43.499 --> 04:45.417
Hey, uncle sent some more...

04:45.626 --> 04:46.709
Huh!?

04:46.710 --> 04:47.628
I see.

04:48.754 --> 04:50.881
Eh... sashimi?

04:51.006 --> 04:52.465
Thanks, Iori-kun.

04:52.466 --> 04:55.135
Sorry, my hands
are full right now.

04:55.261 --> 04:56.846
Chisa, come here for a sec.

04:57.054 --> 04:58.680
Huh? Ah... okay.

04:58.681 --> 04:59.682
Ah, no.

05:00.891 --> 05:02.433
J-Just so you know,

05:02.434 --> 05:04.644
that was just some
prank between girls...

05:04.645 --> 05:05.186
Chisa.

05:05.187 --> 05:06.397
W-What?

05:06.897 --> 05:09.316
You might not realize it,

05:09.733 --> 05:12.193
but the situation just
now was a bit dangerous.

05:12.194 --> 05:13.445
What are you on about?

05:15.865 --> 05:18.659
Anyway, don't talk about
things like that anymore.

05:19.785 --> 05:22.288
Seriously, he doesn't
make any sense.

05:22.580 --> 05:24.290
Chii-chan, is this a movie?

05:24.707 --> 05:26.583
IN A LIMITLESS BLUE It's
a documentary about diving.

05:26.584 --> 05:28.085
IN A LIMITLESS BLUE It
must be your favorite one.

05:28.460 --> 05:31.254
I lent it to Iori, and he
just returned it yesterday.

05:31.255 --> 05:33.591
Wow, I want to watch it too.

05:34.425 --> 05:35.133
Phew.

05:35.134 --> 05:36.677
Oh, Iori.

05:36.927 --> 05:38.887
Senpai, when did you get here?

05:38.888 --> 05:41.639
There's no porn inside.

05:41.640 --> 05:42.808
Really?

05:43.017 --> 05:46.102
Sorry, I must've put
the wrong disc in.

05:46.103 --> 05:48.396
Seriously? Come on man.

05:48.397 --> 05:50.398
By the way, what disc is inside?

05:50.399 --> 05:52.318
Ah, a movie about diving...

06:03.787 --> 06:06.415
Was that the hand signal
for "I'm descending?"

06:06.707 --> 06:09.335
No, it's just a
notice of execution.

06:14.673 --> 06:15.673
Well...

06:15.674 --> 06:19.720
it'd be such a waste to just
watch a movie at a girls' party.

06:19.970 --> 06:21.931
Stop being so
flipping considerate!

06:22.097 --> 06:25.058
I'm fine with watching
the rest of that.

06:25.059 --> 06:26.727
That's a bit...

06:26.894 --> 06:29.730
Enough, what a girls' party
really needs is love talk.

06:29.897 --> 06:31.315
Woo!

06:32.525 --> 06:34.527
Then let's talk about love.

06:34.985 --> 06:35.944
NOT INTERESTED

06:35.945 --> 06:36.778
DANGER - KEEP AWAY

06:36.779 --> 06:38.239
NO EXPERIENCE

06:38.781 --> 06:41.115
Azusa-san, you go first.

06:41.116 --> 06:42.575
Huh, me?

06:42.576 --> 06:45.204
You seem to have
a lot of experience.

06:45.329 --> 06:48.122
Mmm, that's a tough
one to answer on the spot.

06:48.123 --> 06:49.874
Something recent, maybe?

06:49.875 --> 06:51.209
Something recent?

06:51.210 --> 06:52.670
Recently...

06:52.836 --> 06:54.797
I invited Iori to have sex.

06:56.257 --> 06:58.759
W-W-What?

06:59.635 --> 07:01.387
And then what happened?

07:01.887 --> 07:03.764
I got rejected.

07:05.099 --> 07:08.269
Azusa-san, could
it be... you like Iori?

07:08.435 --> 07:09.019
Huh?

07:09.687 --> 07:11.564
Mmm, I do.

07:14.108 --> 07:16.025
What about you, Aina?

07:16.026 --> 07:17.944
Huh!? I-I'm uh...?!

07:17.945 --> 07:19.779
Anyway, let's drink.

07:19.780 --> 07:21.447
It's a girls' party, after all.

07:21.448 --> 07:22.908
Aha, she runs away.

07:23.075 --> 07:24.284
Cheers!

07:24.285 --> 07:26.036
Yeah, cheers!

07:31.667 --> 07:34.168
Is Nanaka-san weak at drinking?

07:34.169 --> 07:36.379
I don't think she's very strong.

07:36.380 --> 07:37.798
Oh, that's right.

07:38.966 --> 07:41.927
Here, entrance tickets
for my uni's festival.

07:42.094 --> 07:44.138
Oh, you need tickets to get in?

07:44.346 --> 07:46.639
It's to keep out the weirdos.

07:46.640 --> 07:48.725
Getting hit on is annoying.

07:48.726 --> 07:51.978
A famous voice actress
is coming this year too.

07:51.979 --> 07:53.189
I see.

07:53.355 --> 07:55.857
Iori and Kouhei would
probably want to go.

07:55.858 --> 07:57.317
True.

07:57.318 --> 07:59.945
So we have to hide it from them.

08:06.368 --> 08:07.577
Now, Cakey!

08:07.578 --> 08:10.038
If you don't want your
party to get any worse...

08:10.039 --> 08:13.666
then hand over
that ticket quietly.

08:13.667 --> 08:15.126
Absolutely not.

08:15.127 --> 08:15.877
Why not?

08:15.878 --> 08:16.711
Gyaaa!

08:16.712 --> 08:18.630
Do I have to
spell it out for you?

08:18.631 --> 08:20.507
Anyway, I'm not
giving them up at all.

08:20.508 --> 08:21.508
What about yours?

08:21.509 --> 08:23.177
I already gave them all away.

08:23.344 --> 08:26.513
I also gave Chisa
the last ticket.

08:26.514 --> 08:27.431
What?

08:27.640 --> 08:28.765
Is that so?

08:28.766 --> 08:30.350
ADMITS UP TO 4 PEOPLE

08:30.351 --> 08:32.228
Kouhei, block the exit.

08:32.520 --> 08:33.687
Okay.

08:35.397 --> 08:37.608
Hey, Chisa.

08:38.484 --> 08:42.321
There's a debt between
you and I, isn't there?

08:42.571 --> 08:44.406
Well, yes, but...

08:45.157 --> 08:47.826
How could I forget that debt?

08:48.327 --> 08:50.037
You will forgive me?

08:50.204 --> 08:51.247
You owe me one.

08:51.455 --> 08:53.958
Can I put it on my
tab one more time?

08:54.291 --> 08:55.833
You're the one in debt?

08:55.834 --> 08:56.709
What would you do?

08:56.710 --> 08:57.627
Reject it.

08:57.628 --> 08:59.629
Then I'll be your bodyguard.

08:59.630 --> 09:01.422
And I'll be your pack mule.

09:01.423 --> 09:02.507
I don't need it either.

09:02.508 --> 09:04.425
- Please reconsider!
- Please reconsider!

09:04.426 --> 09:06.302
Guys will flirt with
you at the festival.

09:06.303 --> 09:08.888
We'll keep the creeps away.

09:08.889 --> 09:11.684
There are two creeps
following me right now.

09:11.934 --> 09:15.937
By the way, Iori is technically
Chisa's boyfriend, isn't he?

09:15.938 --> 09:16.814
Sh-shit!

09:17.857 --> 09:19.190
Cakey, that's...

09:19.191 --> 09:20.568
W-W-What's wrong?

09:28.909 --> 09:31.620
Thank goodness,
she's completely drunk.

09:31.787 --> 09:33.580
Nanaka, are you okay?

09:33.581 --> 09:35.541
I'm okay.

09:37.167 --> 09:40.253
Is Nanaka-san always
like this when she's drunk?

09:40.254 --> 09:42.755
Yeah, usually when
she gets drunk...

09:42.756 --> 09:44.215
Chisa-chan.

09:44.216 --> 09:46.759
She starts hugging
people like this.

09:46.760 --> 09:47.595
I see.

09:47.720 --> 09:49.345
Sis, it's hot.

09:49.346 --> 09:50.556
Whaa?

09:51.182 --> 09:53.099
Then I'll hug Iori-kun instead.

09:53.100 --> 09:54.560
- Here.
- Huh? Aina?

09:54.685 --> 09:56.604
Then I'll hug Nanaka too.

09:57.146 --> 09:59.814
Nanaka, have yours
gotten bigger again?

09:59.815 --> 10:01.608
Just a little bit.

10:01.609 --> 10:03.776
Sis, I can't breathe.

10:03.777 --> 10:04.778
Huh?

10:06.155 --> 10:09.450
This is a girls' party, so
you boys get the hell out!

10:11.076 --> 10:12.493
Damn you, Cakey!

10:12.494 --> 10:14.038
She's like a tyrant.

10:14.747 --> 10:17.290
That's the first time I've
seen Nanaka-san drunk.

10:17.291 --> 10:20.044
I didn't expect her to have
a habit of hugging people.

10:20.461 --> 10:24.715
Thanks to that, she didn't
notice when Cakey slipped up.

10:25.049 --> 10:28.219
The bigger problem
right now is...

10:28.469 --> 10:30.887
how do we get an
Oumi ticket, right?

10:30.888 --> 10:31.847
Yep.

10:35.935 --> 10:37.477
Good morning.

10:37.478 --> 10:40.940
Oh, breakfast will
be ready in a moment.

10:42.691 --> 10:45.777
By the way, Nanaka-san
is weak to alcohol, right?

10:45.778 --> 10:46.528
She is?

10:46.529 --> 10:47.278
Yes.

10:47.279 --> 10:49.697
She got drunk and hugged
Chisa tightly yesterday.

10:49.698 --> 10:51.116
That's weird.

10:51.450 --> 10:53.244
Weird?

10:53.577 --> 10:56.497
She's my daughter, after all.

10:56.914 --> 10:59.374
Good morning, dad, Iori-kun.

10:59.375 --> 11:02.126
Good morning.

11:02.127 --> 11:02.961
Iori-kun.

11:02.962 --> 11:03.587
Yes?

11:04.421 --> 11:07.299
Yesterday, about you
being Chisa's boyfriend...

11:07.800 --> 11:09.510
tell me all the details later.

11:12.680 --> 11:15.349
There's no way she'd get
drunk from a bit of alcohol.

11:18.018 --> 11:20.979
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 2

11:20.980 --> 11:22.940
IZU UNIVERSITY

11:23.274 --> 11:24.984
BEFORE FIRST PERIOD

11:33.284 --> 11:34.994
BEFORE SECOND PERIOD INTRODUCTION
TO MECHANICAL ENGINEERING

11:38.247 --> 11:39.957
LUNCH BREAK

11:45.880 --> 11:47.006
AFTER CLASSES

11:49.049 --> 11:51.635
Why are there so many of you?!

11:52.344 --> 11:54.679
Seriously, you bastards
are damn annoying.

11:54.680 --> 11:56.557
Have some shame.

11:56.765 --> 12:00.018
Like we could stay quiet after
hearing about the Oumi festival ticket!

12:00.019 --> 12:02.354
People are selling them
at a premium, you know!?

12:02.521 --> 12:04.939
Everyone who doesn't know Chisa,

12:04.940 --> 12:05.608
get lost!

12:06.317 --> 12:08.110
Don't mess with
us! Open the door!

12:08.277 --> 12:09.777
Hold the door!

12:09.778 --> 12:11.655
Unrelated people stay outside!

12:12.031 --> 12:14.657
Your Highness, we
have eliminated the pests.

12:14.658 --> 12:17.328
No, I think there
are still plenty left.

12:17.536 --> 12:19.746
Even after that, there
are still this many?

12:19.747 --> 12:20.664
Way too many.

12:20.831 --> 12:23.583
Only three more people can go.

12:23.584 --> 12:26.170
Meaning, besides me,
there are two more spots.

12:27.671 --> 12:28.880
How should we end this?

12:28.881 --> 12:31.008
How about just
fighting to the death?

12:31.175 --> 12:32.509
I guess we have to.

12:32.510 --> 12:33.594
Wait.

12:35.471 --> 12:37.805
How about we let Chisa choose?

12:37.806 --> 12:38.890
I see.

12:38.891 --> 12:39.766
That's fine.

12:39.767 --> 12:42.185
We're choosing who to
go with Kotegawa after all.

12:42.186 --> 12:43.603
Are you okay with that?

12:43.604 --> 12:44.979
I want to go by my...

12:44.980 --> 12:46.232
Ok! Sounds good.

12:46.565 --> 12:49.068
COMPANION SELECTION INTERVIEW

12:51.195 --> 12:54.531
Listen up, each person only
has two minutes to convince her.

12:54.532 --> 12:55.658
Got it!

12:55.866 --> 12:57.659
- Alright.- I want to go home.

12:57.660 --> 12:58.660
Me first.

12:58.661 --> 13:00.704
CONTESTANT #1: YUU MITARAI

13:01.288 --> 13:03.624
Then I'll be going first.

13:04.375 --> 13:05.501
So it's Mitarai.

13:05.751 --> 13:07.169
What is he planning?

13:07.336 --> 13:11.382
I'll win her over
with sweet talk.

13:11.590 --> 13:12.466
Huh?

13:13.509 --> 13:16.387
Kotegawa-san,
do you like sweets?

13:16.679 --> 13:18.138
Well, I suppose.

13:18.264 --> 13:23.309
Actually, a friend of mine at
Oumi is opening a crepe stand.

13:23.310 --> 13:26.104
There's also taiyaki
and red bean soup.

13:26.105 --> 13:27.564
I can take you there.

13:27.565 --> 13:29.148
Ah, if that's the case...

13:29.149 --> 13:29.817
Yes?

13:30.359 --> 13:33.236
Why not ask that
friend for a ticket?

13:33.237 --> 13:34.153
Crap!

13:34.154 --> 13:34.779
Can't you?

13:34.780 --> 13:35.406
Oh no...

13:35.614 --> 13:37.741
It's true that I
could do that, but...

13:38.158 --> 13:39.534
Huh? Tickets?

13:39.535 --> 13:41.036
Huh? HUH?

13:41.161 --> 13:44.247
Right now, I can't
get in contact with her.

13:44.248 --> 13:45.790
You bastard!

13:45.791 --> 13:47.208
Damn it, you normie.

13:47.209 --> 13:48.626
If you have a way in, use it!

13:48.627 --> 13:51.004
Chisa, you don't
need to pick this jerk!

13:51.005 --> 13:53.006
CONTESTANT #2:
SHINICHIROU YAMAMOTO

13:53.007 --> 13:54.799
I'm going next.

13:54.800 --> 13:57.428
Huh? What's with
that confident look?

13:58.345 --> 14:01.598
I will use my sincerity
to win her sympathy.

14:01.599 --> 14:03.057
A direct approach?

14:03.058 --> 14:05.644
No trickery might help
to score him some points.

14:08.314 --> 14:09.230
Kotegawa-san.

14:09.231 --> 14:10.356
Y-Yes?

14:10.357 --> 14:13.359
I'm betting everything
on the Oumi festival that...

14:13.360 --> 14:15.945
I will get a girlfriend.

14:15.946 --> 14:17.906
I-I see...

14:17.907 --> 14:18.740
No, it's hopeless.

14:18.741 --> 14:19.950
Impossible.

14:20.117 --> 14:23.536
But if you refuse,
I will give up.

14:23.537 --> 14:25.955
- But in exchange...
- Huh?

14:25.956 --> 14:28.918
please be my girlfriend.

14:31.420 --> 14:33.047
Don't hand it to him, Chisa!

14:33.172 --> 14:34.714
That's a dirty move, Yamamoto!

14:34.715 --> 14:37.175
That's not sincerity,
but intimidation!

14:37.176 --> 14:40.137
I don't have the luxury of
giving a shit about what you think.

14:41.096 --> 14:43.807
I-I already have
a boyfriend, so...

14:45.017 --> 14:46.226
Stop it, Chisa!

14:46.227 --> 14:48.520
These guys will
hang me on the spot.

14:48.521 --> 14:50.564
CONTESTANT #3: KOUHEI IMAMURA

14:51.106 --> 14:52.398
NEGOTIATIONS WITH HER I'm next.

14:52.399 --> 14:53.733
- Oh.
- What's your plan?

14:53.734 --> 14:55.735
I'm clumsy and not
good with words.

14:55.736 --> 14:57.070
No need for many words.

14:57.071 --> 14:57.779
I see.

14:57.780 --> 14:58.781
Then what'll you do?

14:59.114 --> 15:02.409
I'll let a man's
back do the talking.

15:02.618 --> 15:03.576
What?

15:03.577 --> 15:05.538
Truly befitting of a man.

15:12.670 --> 15:14.547
I can offer up to
two more of these.

15:15.047 --> 15:16.965
What part of that
is a man's back!?

15:16.966 --> 15:19.175
Not a mound of masculinity.

15:19.176 --> 15:21.595
Pretty talk won't get me
into a seiyuu's concert.

15:22.304 --> 15:24.181
Bribing with money is a bit...

15:24.849 --> 15:26.099
Well said, Chisa.

15:26.100 --> 15:27.350
How about this life of mine?

15:27.351 --> 15:29.227
I'll offer up my life.

15:29.228 --> 15:30.645
Don't be a sore loser.

15:30.646 --> 15:32.438
Get lost, you piece of shit!

15:32.439 --> 15:34.441
CONTESTANT #4: HAJIME NOJIMA

15:34.817 --> 15:38.487
Let me show you guys an
example of how to seduce a woman.

15:43.701 --> 15:46.704
Well, Kotegawa-san, you
are as beautiful as always.

15:46.996 --> 15:49.289
The reason I'm trying
this hard is because...

15:49.290 --> 15:51.291
I don't want someone
as gorgeous as you...

15:51.292 --> 15:54.378
to have to go with those
filthy pieces of trash.

15:54.837 --> 15:56.796
You're like a sleeping princess.

15:56.797 --> 15:59.175
If I were a prince,
I would always...

16:00.217 --> 16:00.885
Huh?

16:01.302 --> 16:03.012
Ah, sorry, give me a second.

16:08.851 --> 16:09.685
Uh...

16:10.019 --> 16:11.019
please continue.

16:11.020 --> 16:12.896
Ah no, I'm... already finished.

16:12.897 --> 16:15.648
That was a top-tier
example, Nojima.

16:15.649 --> 16:17.025
Honestly like a joke!

16:17.026 --> 16:19.236
"If I were a prince,"
and then what?

16:19.612 --> 16:22.114
Shut up! If it weren't
for that text message...

16:24.074 --> 16:25.867
Was it you!?

16:25.868 --> 16:27.535
How pathetic, Nojima.

16:27.536 --> 16:29.329
Don't blame Kitahara!

16:29.330 --> 16:32.708
It means your seduction is
worse than a text message!

16:32.875 --> 16:34.167
How could that be!

16:34.168 --> 16:35.418
If I'd keep on talking...

16:35.419 --> 16:36.336
Huh?

16:36.337 --> 16:38.339
That was a close call.
Thanks for saving me.

16:38.714 --> 16:40.423
Kotegawa-san!

16:40.424 --> 16:41.967
No, anyone would do that.

16:42.384 --> 16:45.804
But you really
don't pull any punch.

16:45.930 --> 16:47.640
Why are you so desperate?

16:47.848 --> 16:50.017
Well, I have my reasons.

16:50.976 --> 16:52.228
That's what happened.

16:52.478 --> 16:55.147
I'm only acting as
Chisa's boyfriend.

16:59.777 --> 17:01.987
So that's what it was.

17:05.991 --> 17:09.827
I was wondering what I would
do if you two were really dating.

17:09.828 --> 17:12.956
I wouldn't dare to ask
what you would've done.

17:12.957 --> 17:15.667
So Iori, if that's the case...

17:15.668 --> 17:16.252
Yes?

17:16.377 --> 17:21.090
Chisa-chan wouldn't get
hit on at Oumi Festival, right?

17:22.258 --> 17:24.634
My life is on the line.

17:24.635 --> 17:26.720
I absolutely cannot
screw this up.

17:26.929 --> 17:29.013
Hey, you're next, Kitahara.

17:29.014 --> 17:31.266
Hurry up and fail already.

17:31.267 --> 17:33.269
CONTESTANT #5: IORI KITAHARA

17:34.895 --> 17:35.436
Huh?

17:35.437 --> 17:36.020
Heh?

17:36.021 --> 17:37.356
What is that guy doing?

17:38.607 --> 17:40.568
Chisa, choose me.

17:40.818 --> 17:42.528
I'm also doing
this for your sake.

17:42.778 --> 17:45.030
Why would it be for my sake?

17:45.364 --> 17:46.824
Think about it carefully.

17:47.283 --> 17:51.077
You don't want to have a corpse
and a murderer in your house, right?

17:51.078 --> 17:52.830
Wait, what do you mean by that?

17:53.247 --> 17:56.040
Does that mean you'd
go as far as to kill me?

17:56.041 --> 17:57.334
Don't misunderstand.

17:57.459 --> 17:58.878
The corpse would be me.

17:59.211 --> 18:00.796
And the culprit is Nanaka-san.

18:01.255 --> 18:04.048
Why does this involve my sister?

18:04.049 --> 18:05.968
Ah, that's because...

18:06.427 --> 18:09.846
Nanaka-san is a siscon
who is obsessively into you.

18:09.847 --> 18:11.431
Huh? Is that true?

18:11.432 --> 18:14.476
I'm sorry my sister
is such a huge siscon!

18:15.686 --> 18:17.146
That would never happen.

18:17.646 --> 18:18.355
Huh?

18:18.564 --> 18:20.691
I can't tell you the
reason, but please...

18:20.858 --> 18:22.150
choose me!

18:22.151 --> 18:22.734
No.

18:22.735 --> 18:25.486
Okay, then I'll do
anything you want.

18:25.487 --> 18:28.198
Then get run over five
times and then give up.

18:28.199 --> 18:30.366
I would be dead by that time!

18:30.367 --> 18:32.243
Chisa, I'm doing this for you!

18:32.244 --> 18:33.828
Oops, time's up.

18:33.829 --> 18:35.663
It's been over two minutes.

18:35.664 --> 18:36.956
Hurry up and get back.

18:36.957 --> 18:38.374
Chisa! Chisa!!

18:38.375 --> 18:40.460
CONTESTANT #6: KENTA FUJIWARA

18:40.461 --> 18:42.338
Then I'm the last one.

18:42.588 --> 18:44.089
Oh, you're still here.

18:44.256 --> 18:48.009
This guy barely talks to Kotegawa
and doesn't have any likeable traits.

18:48.010 --> 18:49.470
He's sure to lose.

18:50.638 --> 18:52.556
If I get to go with you...

18:53.098 --> 18:54.349
I will do nothing.

18:54.350 --> 18:55.309
- Huh?
- What?

18:55.809 --> 18:58.646
If you'd just let me
in, I'll leave you alone.

18:58.812 --> 19:00.898
I won't cause any
trouble on my own, either.

19:01.315 --> 19:03.817
I swear I won't get in your way.

19:04.401 --> 19:06.987
Crap, so that's how it was.

19:07.154 --> 19:10.157
Chisa doesn't care about
what we would do for her.

19:10.658 --> 19:12.117
What important is...

19:12.785 --> 19:15.246
what we wouldn't do for her!

19:16.747 --> 19:18.958
What do you think, Kotegawa-san?

19:19.166 --> 19:20.875
If that's the case, then...

19:20.876 --> 19:21.876
We've been had.

19:21.877 --> 19:23.419
That guy's the most cunning one.

19:23.420 --> 19:25.130
How can we win against that!

19:25.339 --> 19:27.675
How can I give up so easily.

19:28.175 --> 19:30.177
These guys are
just in it for the girls.

19:30.386 --> 19:33.222
If it's not possible,
they can just give up.

19:33.764 --> 19:35.057
But I'm...

19:36.976 --> 19:39.310
I'm carrying a different burden!

19:39.311 --> 19:41.772
Oops, my elbow slipped...

19:43.315 --> 19:45.317
You bastard!

19:45.484 --> 19:46.610
Just as I thought.

19:46.944 --> 19:49.821
I knew what you
were trying to do...

19:49.822 --> 19:50.698
already!

19:56.829 --> 19:58.706
Hmph, my apologies.

19:59.081 --> 19:59.873
My hand slipped...

19:59.874 --> 20:03.376
and I pressed a handkerchief
soaked in chemicals into your face.

20:03.377 --> 20:05.880
Well, that can't be helped then.

20:06.046 --> 20:07.463
T-These guys...

20:07.464 --> 20:09.341
Just how desperate are they?

20:09.967 --> 20:12.385
But it's simple now.

20:12.386 --> 20:15.096
All we need to do
is kill everyone else!

20:15.097 --> 20:17.599
We should have
done this from the start.

20:17.600 --> 20:18.933
Bring it on!

20:18.934 --> 20:21.478
I'm betting my
life on this battle.

20:21.645 --> 20:23.647
Well, I'll be going...

20:24.190 --> 20:26.859
Wait, it's pointless
to try to escape.

20:27.318 --> 20:29.485
We'll finish really
soon, just wait there.

20:29.486 --> 20:30.820
Bring it on!

20:30.821 --> 20:31.821
Take this!

20:31.822 --> 20:34.365
- My hand slipped again!
- You bastard!

20:34.366 --> 20:35.783
You're good!

20:35.784 --> 20:36.826
Die!

20:36.827 --> 20:38.036
Bastard!

20:38.037 --> 20:39.120
Just die!

20:39.121 --> 20:40.206
Stop!

20:40.748 --> 20:43.417
As I thought, we
shouldn't do this.

20:43.667 --> 20:47.546
How could close friends
fight over something like this?

20:48.297 --> 20:50.965
Friends should be
equal with each other.

20:50.966 --> 20:54.637
It isn't right for some to get
an advantage over the rest.

20:55.471 --> 20:56.597
I believe that...

20:56.805 --> 21:01.768
everyone here is not the
type to fight among friends.

21:01.769 --> 21:03.186
Kotegawa-san.

21:03.187 --> 21:06.106
Friends have to
be equal and fair?

21:06.565 --> 21:08.317
That's right.

21:08.609 --> 21:10.069
Sorry, Chisa.

21:10.277 --> 21:11.278
Sorry.

21:11.529 --> 21:13.780
I'm glad you understand.

21:13.781 --> 21:15.657
So I'll go alone...

21:15.658 --> 21:17.785
Alright then, guys.

21:18.202 --> 21:20.036
From now on, we're
no longer friends.

21:20.037 --> 21:20.828
Yeah!

21:20.829 --> 21:23.207
Now we can kill each
other with no regrets.

21:24.792 --> 21:27.126
No, that's not it.

21:27.127 --> 21:31.215
I mean, everyone should value friendship
more than what's in front of you.

21:32.216 --> 21:34.176
That's enough!

21:34.969 --> 21:35.718
Oh.

21:35.719 --> 21:36.678
What's up, Mitarai?

21:36.679 --> 21:40.015
It's from my childhood
friend who goes to Oumi.

21:40.182 --> 21:40.932
Geez!

21:40.933 --> 21:42.892
If you want it that badly,
I'll give you a ticket.

21:42.893 --> 21:44.812
Just this once.

21:45.229 --> 21:48.107
If you cheat on me next
time, I'll break your jaw.

21:48.607 --> 21:50.817
She gave me a ticket in the end.

21:50.818 --> 21:51.568
Oho!

21:51.569 --> 21:53.319
So four people can go with that.

21:53.320 --> 21:55.989
Plus Chisa's ticket, that's
more than enough to get in.

21:55.990 --> 21:56.447
4 PEOPLE + 4 PEOPLE = 8 PEOPLE

21:56.448 --> 21:57.366
You're right.

21:57.616 --> 21:58.826
- So that means...
- So that means...

22:03.330 --> 22:04.205
I see.

22:04.206 --> 22:06.916
So everyone will be going
to the Oumi festival together.

22:06.917 --> 22:08.418
Yes we are!

22:08.419 --> 22:11.380
Why do you look so down, Chisa?

22:21.557 --> 22:23.099
Wanna talk to you,
wanna talk to you

22:23.100 --> 22:24.976
First I gotta know all
about you, isn't that right?

22:24.977 --> 22:26.936
Ending it off at round
one reeks of boredom

22:26.937 --> 22:28.688
Rounds two, three,
and four is the plan

22:28.689 --> 22:30.398
As the night gets deeper,
true thoughts escape

22:30.399 --> 22:32.317
Let us go on and on
and dive down late

22:32.318 --> 22:35.320
Your history, your scenery, for
me will your pages get slippery

22:35.321 --> 22:37.363
Hey, show me even more

22:37.364 --> 22:39.115
This is my track and
you are the featured guest

22:39.116 --> 22:40.700
We'll forget by the
time when the dawn hits

22:40.701 --> 22:42.160
Being incomplete is perfection

22:42.161 --> 22:44.412
Hey, show me even more

22:44.413 --> 22:45.997
My mouth keeps slipping,
my mouth keeps slipping

22:45.998 --> 22:47.624
Complaint whether
we sober upward

22:47.625 --> 22:49.668
For now, let's ride
high on this feeling

22:50.044 --> 22:56.091
Let's live this moment with all we
can without leaving a single regret,

22:56.592 --> 22:58.301
We are gonna do it,
we go past the limit now

22:58.302 --> 22:59.928
Not just the whole night,
party till the sun is out

22:59.929 --> 23:02.096
Let's fly high

23:02.097 --> 23:02.680
(Let's fly high)

23:02.681 --> 23:04.682
So first, you just strip it down

23:04.683 --> 23:06.976
An exposed and
feral kind of bond

23:06.977 --> 23:10.605
It's the way of life's cycle,
let us go way beyond

23:10.606 --> 23:12.232
The very moment that
we met I drop my shy act

23:12.233 --> 23:13.983
I wanna bare it all and
say what I need to say

23:13.984 --> 23:15.986
Do it now...

23:16.779 --> 23:21.074
This is the magic spell that breaks
down each and every single wall

23:21.075 --> 23:24.536
And once you get used to
it, you won't feel a thing at all

23:24.537 --> 23:26.037
Being without clothes
is a mystery I live in

23:26.038 --> 23:27.789
The drinking and chatting
is flowing more freely

23:27.790 --> 23:30.167
Try it now...

23:30.584 --> 23:34.087
And right before you
realize what's going on

23:34.088 --> 23:38.300
Your heart will catch
right up and finally be free

23:44.932 --> 23:49.937
NEXT TIME: FIRST TIME
AT A WOMEN'S COLLEGE
